# Assigned cell: mode=menus, view=820x1180,touch, save=carried (#273 means
# this plays as a genuinely fresh origin, not an actual second-evening carry).
#
# Picking up exactly where 2026-09-27-9.play's last note left off: that
# session pressed the fight screen's own corner `map` button while The
# Skyward Deck was still an open, unresolved pull, found the fight kept
# simulating behind the map (hud.time and boss hp both advanced while the
# citadel screen was up), and found `tap back` from there landed on the front
# page rather than back on the fight -- with the live pull still reporting
# `mode=raid outcome=ongoing` on the very same journal line. That session's
# own words: "worth checking on the next session whether pressing RAID from
# that state resumes the live ... pull ... or drops it, before writing the
# fix this deserves." No session has pressed RAID from exactly that state.
# Using Bonegrinder (the only rung a fresh save has open) instead of Skyward
# Deck -- same mechanism, faster to reach.
open
targets
shot home
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:mage:frost
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot arrive-threshold

# A short per-room budget that will not be enough to kill Bonegrinder (every
# prior idle/style reading on this boss at 10-normal needed 84-220s), so
# `evening` should hand back control with the boss room still `ongoing`
# rather than won or lost.
evening idle 60 3
state
shot mid-pull

# Reveal the corner group the documented way (leaveFight()'s own technique:
# the minimap first, since corners are hidden on touch until it is pressed),
# then press map while the boss fight is still live.
tap minimap
tap map
state
shot citadel-mid-fight

tap back
state
shot after-back

# The open question: does this resume the live Bonegrinder pull, or show a
# fresh setup screen / drop the run?
tap raid
state
shot after-raid-retap
targets
